  "query_preview": "..\nToday through Monday: A dry air mass will remain over the Inland\nNW through Sunday night with precipitatable water values ranging\nfrom near 40-70 percent of normal. This combined with light winds\nwill promote strong radiational cooling with areas of frost. A\nFrost Advisory remains in effect through 9 AM this morning for areas\nstill within their climatological growing season where areas of\nfrost are forecast. For the northern mountain valleys and ID\nPanhandle the average first frost occurs around September \n15th-25th and thus the reason for no advisories since frost is \nmore common this time of year, although many areas still have not \nreceived their first frost yet, with another cool night in store \nfor Sunday Night. For high temperatures gradual warming is \nexpected for Sunday and Monday as southwest flow develops ahead of\nthe next system. High temperatures on Monday will be right near \nnormal values with readings in the mid 60s to low 70s.\n\nMonday Night and Tuesday: A weak atmospheric river takes aim at\nthe region with an increase in moisture as precipitable water\nincreases to 150-200 percent of normal. Yet with the strong\nwesterly flow and dry air mass to start, precipitation will have a\nhard time reaching the ground other than potential sprinkles, and\na chance for light rain over the northern mountains. Upslope flow\ninto the Cascade crest will lead to wet conditions with around\n0.50-1.00 inch of rain, with light rain spilling over the crest\ninto the upper reaches of the Methow Valley, Lake Chelan, and Lake\nWenatchee.\n\nWednesday through Saturday: Following Tuesday's influx of clouds\nand areas of light rain or sprinkles, the weather looks very \nquiet for the rest of the week. A mild west-southwest flow \npattern occurs for the rest of the week with weak ridging bringing\nnear to slightly above normal temperatures. About 25 percent of\nthe model clusters show the stronger ridge building in sooner, by\nFriday, which would result in a more rapid warming trend by\nSaturday if realized. JW",
